RXŠr¦gã8DŸ:çXLAbl_„>Dyòö@JA{"rendered":{"html":"<p>The GCSL language server supplies diagnostics and navigation from the same\nchecker that runs programs. You can use it in an editor that supports the\nLanguage Server Protocol (LSP) over standard input and standard output.</p>\n<h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#before-you-start\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>You need the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>An editor with configurable LSP support.</li>\n<li>The <code>gcsl</code> executable on the editor's command search path.</li>\n<li>A GCSL file or workspace to open.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"connect-the-server\">Connect the server <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#connect-the-server\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Associate files ending in <code>.gcsl</code> with a GCSL language entry in your\neditor.</li>\n<li>Set the server command to <code>gcsl</code> and its argument list to <code>[\"lsp\"]</code>.\nUse standard input and standard output for transport.</li>\n<li>Open a GCSL file. For a multifile project, open the workspace directory\nso the editor can supply file changes and watch notifications.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"check-the-result\">Check the result <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#check-the-result\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Hover over a declared name to see its type. Introduce a misspelled name and\nconfirm that the editor displays a diagnostic. When an unambiguous\nspelling suggestion is available, a quick fix offers the replacement.</p>\n<p>The server checks source but does not evaluate programs. It supports\ncompletion, signature help, inlay hints, formatting, symbol search, and\nreferences. Rename checks the proposed edits before returning them and\nrefuses changes that introduce errors or change name resolution. It does\nnot rename files, directories, or standard-library declarations.</p>\n<h2 id=\"incomplete-source\">Incomplete source <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#incomplete-source\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The index retains useful information around many syntax errors. For an\nunbalanced block, a query can use a repaired copy to answer navigation or\ncompletion while diagnostics still describe the real text. Rename needs\nthe real source to be valid enough to verify and can be refused instead.</p>\n<p>Editor syntax highlighting is a separate integration. The grammar and\nqueries in <code>tree-sitter-gcsl</code> are maintained in their own repository; they\nare not required for the <code>gcsl lsp</code> process to check your code.</p>\n","toc":[{"level":2,"id":"before-you-start","title":"Before you start","number":null},{"level":2,"id":"connect-the-server","title":"Connect the server","number":null},{"level":2,"id":"check-the-result","title":"Check the result","number":null},{"level":2,"id":"incomplete-source","title":"Incomplete source","number":null}],"has_mermaid":false,"dangling":[],"warnings":[],"broken":[]},"images":[],"links":{"pages":[],"anchors":[]},"refs":[]}